			"Message": "docs(Common): Condense README to benefit-focused overview\n\nSimplify the Common crate README from verbose technical documentation to a concise, benefit-oriented overview. Replace 150+ lines of detailed architecture explanations, code examples, and getting started guides with bullet points emphasizing key value propositions: pure abstract traits, compile-time enforcement, and millisecond tests.\n\nKey changes:\n- Add VS Code comparison blockquote: \"VS Code's codebase imports concrete implementations directly...\"\n- Switch Rust icon from cdn.simpleicons.org to editor.land/Image/Rust.svg (branded asset)\n- Remove detailed \"ActionEffect System Explained\" with code samples\n- Remove \"Core Architecture Principles\" table\n- Remove \"Getting Started\" section with installation/usage examples\n- Condense mermaid diagram to simpler \"In the Ecosystem\" section\n- Update \"See Also\" links to point to editor.land documentation\n\nThe README now serves as a quick onboarding anchor point with links to detailed docs rather than a self-contained tutorial.",
